<title>CANADA: Rogers/Cogeco Cable deal okayed.</title>
<headline>Rogers/Cogeco Cable deal okayed.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian regulatory authorities said on Thursday that they have approved Cogeco Cable Inc's bid to buy some of the Ontario cable systems holdings of Rogers Communications Inc.</p>
<p>Rogers agreed last October to sell some Ontario cable sytems for C$350 million to Quebec-based Cogeco Cable.</p>
<p>The systems serve 300,000 subscribers in Hamilton, Niagara Falls, St. Catharines, Sarnia, Wallaceburg, Peterborough, the Ottawa Valley, Cornwall and North Bay.</p>
<p>Regulatory approval means Cogeco will become the fourth largest operator of multiple cable systems in Canada, serving about 750,000 subscribers, the Canadian Radio-television and Telecommunications Commission said in a statement explaining its approval.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613 235-6745))</p>
